.TH SDL_BITSPERPIXEL 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_BITSPERPIXEL \- A macro to determine an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat \(aqs
bits per pixel.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pixels.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_BITSPERPIXEL(format) \(rs
.BI "    (SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_FOURCC(format) ? 0 : (((format) >> 8) & 0xFF))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that this macro double-evaluates its parameter, so do not use expressions with side-effects here\[char46]
.PP
FourCC formats will report zero here, as it rarely makes sense to measure them per-pixel\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I format
an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
to check\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the bits-per-pixel of
.BR format \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_BYTESPERPIXEL (3)
